Maybe both. It seems your biggest problem is the asphynx, which could
stone you. I'm not sure whether they hiss, but aparently it's not a
new moon anymore anyway. In any case, do you have any lizards with
you?

The blinking eye should not be a a problem if you can blind yourself,
which would make it harder to deal with the Golem.

I'd say finish the mine, collect wands and lizards, ID your stuff, and
then come back ready to kill stuff from a distance. Offensive wands
would be nice, but even a wand of sleep would help you be alone with
the golem for a while. Trying for Mojo might be a good idea, even
though you don't have GoP. No reason not to try, at least, if you have
a wand of CM or something. Is minetown's altar coaligned?

Once you finish the mines you should be able to use the gems to rob
the shopkeepers blind and buy at least one level of protection. ID the
gems and then put them in your bag, get a pet and have it steal the
bag. But your AC seems ok for so early in the game.

I'd say, fight the golem by itself, preferably from afar, zapping the
scare wand at the others until you can deal with them, and zapping
yourself with healing. It doesn't look all that bad to me, just be
careful and stay near the stairs.

Quaffing a potion of speed would also help in that little battle, even
if you decide to just run for it.

